## Why This Question Is Asked
This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design tenant-scoped anomaly detection using incremental dbt models, custom macros, and robust CI gates in a multi-tenant Snowflake environment.

## Key Concepts
- Incremental dbt modeling scoped per tenant
- Per-tenant statistical summaries (sigma computation)
- CI gates for production safety
- Automated scheduling with Snowflake TASKS

## Code Example
```javascript
// macros/analytics_base.sql
{% macro compute_sigma(tenant) %}
  {% set stats_table = 'analytics_base.tenant_stats' %}
  SELECT mean, stddev(value) AS sigma
  FROM {{ ref('tenant_events') }}
  WHERE tenant = '{{ tenant }}'
  GROUP BY tenant, event_type
{% endmacro %}

// models/analytics_{{tenant}}/daily_anomalies.sql
{{ config(materialized='incremental', unique_key='date') }}

WITH sigma AS (
  SELECT * FROM {{ analytics_base.compute_sigma(var('tenant')) }}
),
anomalies AS (
  SELECT
    e.tenant,
    DATE(e.event_ts) AS date,
    e.event_type,
    e.value,
    (e.value - s.mean) / NULLIF(s.sigma, 0) AS z_score,
    CASE WHEN ABS((e.value - s.mean) / NULLIF(s.sigma, 0)) > 3 THEN TRUE ELSE FALSE END AS is_anomaly
  FROM {{ ref('staging.tenant_events') }} e
  JOIN sigma s ON e.event_type = s.event_type AND e.tenant = s.tenant
  {% if is_incremental() %}
  WHERE DATE(e.event_ts) > (SELECT MAX(date) FROM {{ this }})
  {% endif %}
)
SELECT * FROM anomalies
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests end-to-end lifecycle management, macro-driven multi-tenant infrastructure, governance capabilities, and auditability. It evaluates proficiency in dynamic object creation, safe removal procedures, data lag handling, and implementing isolation checks.

## Key Concepts
- dbt macros and dynamic SQL generation
- Snowflake object lifecycle management (schemas, grants, drops)
- Tenant lifecycle governance (onboarding/offboarding)
- Row-level security policies and audit trails
- CI validation for per-tenant artifacts and isolation enforcement

## Code Example
```sql
{% macro create_tenant_schema(tenant) %}
  EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS analytics_' ~ tenant;
  {% set grant_stmt %}
    GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA analytics_{{ tenant }} TO ROLE analytics_user;
    GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA analytics_{{ tenant }} TO ROLE analytics_user;
  {% endset %}
  {% do run_query(grant_stmt) %}
{% endmacro %}
```

## Implementation Considerations
- Schema-drift detection using information_schema comparisons
- 1-day data lag handling with window functions and watermark checks
- Cross-tenant isolation tests using query result validation
- CI pipeline steps to validate tenant status alignment with object existence
- Comprehensive audit logging for all schema changes
